Purpose: production TEST rollout of the accepted hardened Google Drive/Yandex archive runtime, durable ambiguous-finalize telemetry, verified large canonical reads via exact Drive size/SHA256 + Yandex byte-for-byte mirror, WB Advertising M0 live read-only tools, Semantic Advertising V1 historical execution, approved operational Semantic Core routing for WB ORDERS/CURRENT_STOCK, top-level Query Execution Plan V2, Clarification Gate, and Query Execution Controller V1, retaining infra-only multi-dataset/data-catalog/runtime overlays.
Architecture contract: annual dataset CSV files and dataset-specific coverage registries are authoritative on Google Drive; Yandex Object Storage stores job state, immutable candidates, staging/resume state and a byte-for-byte backup; the Apps Script Bridge v3 secret is stored in Yandex Lockbox; no Google OAuth refresh token is stored in Yandex. Shared Google Drive Bridge Protocol v1 is retired for Marketplaces and is not a valid Marketplaces runtime fallback.
Top-level request routing contract: marketplace_query_plan is the first server-side planning step for natural marketplace questions. It first selects source families, then returns marketplace_execution_plan.v2 with independent required source legs, downstream executor, execution status, coverage gate, missing context, forbidden substitutions, blockers and a join policy before lower Semantic Core executes a metric/report/API.
Execution-plan contract: statuses are READY, READY_WITH_GATES, NEEDS_CONTEXT and BLOCKED. READY_WITH_GATES permits reading/validation to begin but never means answer completeness is already proven. Every required leg must pass its own gate; a missing required leg blocks the final joined answer. Independent legs may run in parallel only after validation. Cross-source arithmetic or derived business calculations are forbidden without a separate explicit approved Semantic contract, and provenance must remain attached to every leg.
Clarification contract: after marketplace_query_plan and before any data executor, NEEDS_CONTEXT, semantic AMBIGUOUS, semantic UNKNOWN, or an unresolved source class caused by unidentified business meaning enters CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED. ChatGPT/Codex must explain the uncertainty in normal language and ask only for the missing or ambiguous business meaning/context; no data leg may execute. After the user answers, marketplace_query_plan is called again from the top with preserved known marketplace/seller/period/product context. Recognized multi-source requests are not clarification cases merely because they have several legs, while a clearly understood request with a genuinely unavailable source is reported as a source gap instead of receiving a meaningless clarification question.
Execution-controller contract: after a READY or READY_WITH_GATES plan, marketplace_execution_control is the canonical server-side owner of lower executor arguments. It rebuilds the source plan from the user request/context and emits marketplace_leg_execution.v1 contracts containing the exact executor, exact arguments, narrow semantic target, source status/family, coverage gate, forbidden substitutions and provenance requirements. A compound multi-source question is never copied unchanged into multiple executors. If any required leg cannot receive a deterministic contract, dispatch_contracts is empty and no other required leg may run as a partial answer. Client-side rewriting/broadening of executor arguments is forbidden. Join remains fail-closed and arithmetic remains forbidden until an explicit approved calculation contract exists.
Historical availability contract: there is currently no verified populated WB historical orders archive and no historical stock archive. Recent WB orders may use the operational Statistics Orders API only inside its supported retention window; older order history fails closed. Historical stock fails closed and today's snapshot is never substituted. Public marketplace/card facts remain separate from private seller-cabinet facts.
Semantic contract: marketplace_business_query receives the original natural-language question for direct single-route use; source-independent dimensions are normalized before source selection; approved historical capabilities execute only when FULL_COVERAGE is proven; approved operational business metrics may use their explicit live/operational sources; currencies and unrelated financial components are never silently combined; unsupported/current-state/ambiguous concepts fail closed. For controlled execution, lower business-query calls receive the controller-owned narrow per-leg question rather than the original compound request.
Operational Semantic contract: ordinary WB ORDERS requests, including today, route to the approved operational Statistics Orders source but are not complete-order-flow truth. CURRENT_STOCK is a seller-aware live WB snapshot; Base-token cabinets may use the official asynchronous warehouse-remains report; any past-date stock request fails closed before provider access and never receives today's snapshot.
Advertising Semantic contract: closed historical WB cabinet-level advertising_performance reads canonical ads_campaign_daily only after dataset_coverage_registry.csv plus ads_campaign_roster_snapshots prove roster/fullstats FULL_COVERAGE for every expected eligible campaign. Product/nm_id, specific-campaign and campaign-breakdown requests remain fail-closed until separate approved contracts exist; current-day advertising remains live-only.
Advertising metric boundary: wb_ads_m0.v1 metrics, including DRR/ROAS, are WB advertising-attribution operational metrics and must never be presented as complete seller orders, realized seller revenue, overall business profit or full financial result.
Large-file contract: Apps Script Bridge v3 brokers official Google Drive API resumable-session creation; Yandex uploads bounded chunks directly to a deterministic non-canonical staging filename, trusts Drive-confirmed offsets, verifies exact size + Drive SHA256, writes the byte-for-byte Yandex backup, then uses archive-root-scoped promote_verified to replace canonical. Large annual CSVs are never transported through Apps Script as one base64 POST. Canonical content reads first prove the Drive file identity, size and SHA256, then may consume the exact matching Yandex byte-for-byte mirror so large file bytes do not traverse Apps Script; any missing/stale/unverifiable mirror fails closed to the canonical Drive content path.
Recovery contract: unusable non-rate-limit 4xx resumable sessions restart from the immutable candidate; ambiguous 408/5xx query the Drive-confirmed offset before resend; rate limits use bounded backoff/Retry-After; resumable session URIs are bearer-like and must never be logged or returned.
Finalize telemetry contract: every finance finalize keeps durable non-secret correlation evidence for job/report identity, candidate object ID + bytes/SHA256, staging/canonical file IDs, Drive-confirmed resumable offset and bounded phase/event history. Existing in-flight jobs are retrofitted deterministically; session URIs, tokens and secrets are excluded from status telemetry.
Production overlays: preserve the multi-dataset marketplace_data_catalog/marketplace_metric_route layer, Bridge v3 archive controls, runtime service-account authentication, Redis limiter and other accepted infra hardening. Query Execution Plan V2, Clarification Gate, Query Execution Controller V1, Semantic Advertising and operational Semantic Core are layered on top rather than replacing those controls.
Advertising archive contract: Advertising Archive V1 is implemented in the canonical Google Drive archive. Semantic V1 executes cabinet totals from ads_campaign_daily with ads_campaign_roster_snapshots as the coverage dependency; ads_product_daily exists as archive data but has no approved Semantic execution contract yet.
Security contract: Promotion start/pause/stop are WRITE and delete is DESTRUCTIVE at MCP level even though WB exposes them as HTTP GET operations. Current accepted advertising tools remain read-only.
